C. RELIEVING UNEMPLOYMENT;
D. PROVIDING RECREATIONAL AND LEISURE TIME ACTIVITY ON THE INTEREST OF SOCIAL WELFARE FOR PEOPLE LIVING IN THE AREA OF BENEFIT WHO HAVE NEED BY REASON OF THEIR YOUTH, AGE, INFIRMITY OR DISABILITY, POVERTY OR SOCIAL AND ECONOMIC CIRCUMSTANCES WITH A VIEW TO IMPROVING THE CONDITIONS OF LIFE OF SUCH PERSONS.

TO ACT AS A RESOURCE FOR CHILDREN AND YOUNG PEOPLE AGED 6-18 LIVING IN HACKNEY, ISLINGTON, NEWHAM, TOWER HAMLETS AND WALTHAM FOREST BY PROVIDING ADVICE AND ASSISTANCE AND ORGANISING PROGRAMMES OF PHYSICAL, EDUCATIONAL AND OTHER ACTIVITIES AS A MEANS OF:

(A) ADVANCING IN LIFE AND HELPING YOUNG PEOPLE BY DEVELOPING THEIR SKILLS, CAPACITIES AND CAPABILITIES TO ENABLE THEM TO PARTICIPATE IN SOCIETY AS INDEPENDENT, MATURE AND RESPONSIBLE INDIVIDUALS;

(B) ADVANCING EDUCATION;

(C) PROVIDING RECREATIONAL AND LEISURE TIME ACTIVITIES IN THE INTEREST OF SOCIAL WELFARE, DESIGNED TO IMPROVE THEIR CONDITIONS OF LIFE.

THE CHARITY'S OBJECTS ("OBJECTS") ARE SPECIFICALLY RESTRICTED TO THE FOLLOWING:

(1) SUBJECT AS PROVIDED IN SUB-CLAUSE (2) OF THIS ARTICLE, TO PROMOTE SUCH CHARITABLE PURPOSES AS FALL WITHIN THE DESCRIPTIONS:

(A) THE PREVENTION OR RELIEF OF POVERTY;
(B) THE ADVANCEMENT OF EDUCATION;
(C) THE ADVANCEMENT OF RELIGION;
(D) THE ADVANCEMENT OF HEALTH OR THE SAVING OF LIVES;
(E) THE ADVANCEMENT OF THE ARTS, CULTURE, HERITAGE OR SCIENCE;
(F) THE ADVANCEMENT OF AMATEUR SPORT;
(G) THE PROMOTION OF RELIGIOUS OR RACIAL HARMONY OR EQUALITY AND DIVERSITY;
(H) THE ADVANCEMENT OF ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION OR IMPROVEMENT; AND
(I) THE RELIEF OF THOSE IN NEED BECAUSE OF YOUTH, AGE, ILL-HEALTH, DISABILITY, FINANCIAL HARDSHIP OR OTHER DISADVANTAGE.

(2) THE CHARITY SHALL, INITIALLY AND PRIMARILY, SEEK TO ATTAIN ITS OBJECTS FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE PRIMARY BENEFICIARIES. IF THE TRUSTEES DETERMINE THAT THERE ARE INSUFFICIENT PRIMARY BENEFICIARIES, THEY MAY DETERMINE THAT THE CHARITY SHALL SEEK TO ATTAIN ITS OBJECTS FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE SECONDARY BENEFICIARIES. IF THE TRUSTEES DETERMINE THAT THERE ARE INSUFFICIENT SECONDARY BENEFICIARIES, THEY MAY DETERMINE, SUBJECT TO ARTICLE 46(5), THAT THE CHARITY SHALL SEEK TO ATTAIN ITS OBJECTS FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE TERTIARY BENEFICIARIES.

3.1 THE COMPANY'S OBJECTS (THE "OBJECTS") ARE SPECIFICALLY RESTRICTED TO THE FOLLOWING: 
3.1.1 THE ADVANCEMENT OF EDUCATION FOR THE PUBLIC BENEFIT IN AND THROUGH MEMBER SCHOOLS AND OTHER EDUCATIONAL SETTINGS AND INITIATIVES IN THE UNITED KINGDOM, WITH AN INITIAL FOCUS ON THE LONDON BOROUGH OF TOWER HAMLETS, INCLUDING BY:
(A) ENABLING SCHOOLS TO WORK TOGETHER TO IMPROVE THEMSELVES AND EACH OTHER; 
(B) PROMOTING THE QUALITY OF TEACHING AND LEARNING; 
(C) PROVIDING OR PROCURING SCHOOL IMPROVEMENT SERVICES TO MEMBER SCHOOLS;
(D) PROVIDING OPPORTUNITIES FOR DEVELOPMENT AND LEARNING OF STAFF, GOVERNORS AND PARENTS AT MEMBER SCHOOLS, AND OF STAFF AND DIRECTORS OF THE COMPANY;
(E) MAINTAINING AND ANALYSING RESULTS AND PERFORMANCE OF PUPILS, SCHOOLS AND OTHER EDUCATIONAL SETTINGS AND INITIATIVES; AND
(F) PROVIDING OR PROCURING OTHER SERVICES TO SCHOOLS AND OTHER EDUCATIONAL SETTINGS AND INITIATIVES; AND
3.1.2 THE PROMOTION OF ANY OTHER CHARITABLE PURPOSE AS THE DIRECTORS MAY DETERMINE FROM TIME TO TIME.

THE DEVELOPMENT AND EDUCATION OF CHILDREN AND YOUNG PEOPLE IN PARTICULAR BY:
PROMOTING THEIR CARE AND SAFETY;
PROMOTING THEIR EDUCATION AND PROMOTING PARENTAL INVOLVEMENT;
PROMOTING THEIR HEALTH AND WELLBEING;
PROVIDING SERVICES TO SUPPORT THEM AND THEIR FAMILIES AND CARERS;
PROVIDING SERVICES TO INDIVIDUALS HOLDING MEMBERSHIP OF THE CIO; AND
FURTHERING THE AIMS OF THE PRE SCHOOL LEARNING ALLIANCE.

THE CHARITY'S OBJECTS ARE SPECIFICALLY RESTRICTED TO THE FOLLOWING: 
1. THE ADVANCEMENT OF THE PERFORMING ARTS, SPECIFICALLY MUSIC, FOR THE PUBLIC BENEFIT, IN PARTICULAR BUT NOT EXCLUSIVELY BYÙ
A)PROVIDING A PROGRAMME OF PUBLIC PERFORMANCES DEVOTED TO NEW MUSIC; 
B)PROVIDING A DEDICATED FORUM FOR RESEARCH IN ORDER TO FURTHER DIALOGUE WITHIN THE NEW MUSIC COMMUNITY; 
C)PROVIDING PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT AND PERFORMANCE OPPORTUNITIES FOR ARTISTS IDENTIFYING AS FEMALE, THUS ADVANCING EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES IN AN HISTORICALLY MALE-DOMINATED PROFESSION;
D)PROMOTING THE HIGHEST STANDARDS AND SUPPORTING ENGAGED RISK-TAKING IN THE CREATION AND PERFORMANCE OF NEW MUSICAL WORKS; AND 
2. THE ADVANCEMENT OF THE EDUCATION OF THE PUBLIC IN GENERAL IN THE SUBJECT OF MUSIC, IN PARTICULAR BUT NOT EXCLUSIVELY BY
A)PROMOTING A BROAD AND DIVERSE REPERTOIRE OF NEW MUSIC;
B)PROMOTING INDIVIDUAL AND COLLECTIVE KNOWLEDGE IN THE SPECIFIC AREAS OF LIVE PERFORMANCE, COMMISSIONING AND PROGRAMMING; 
C)RAISING AWARENESS OF THE CHARITYÆS ACTIVITIES THROUGH INFORMATION MEDIA.

THE RELIEF OF SICKNESS AND THE PRESERVATION OF HEALTH AMONG PEOPLE AND THEIR FAMILIES WHO ARE SUFFERING OR AT RISK OF SUFFERING FROM EMOTIONAL, PSYCHOLOGICAL OR MENTAL DISTRESS BY:
THE PROVISION OF SUPPORT IN ORDER TO ALLEVIATE OR PREVENT SUCH SUFFERING OR STIGMA AND;
RAISING AWARENESS THEREOF IN SUCH WAYS AS THE TRUSTEES SHALL FROM TIME TO TIME THINK FIT.

Activities:
The charity promotes arts and culture for the benefit of the public, in part but not exclusively by:
Supporting young performers;
Organising art exhibitions and concerts for the benefit of the public to promote choral music, and;
Creating opportunities for cultural exchange.

Charity Objects:
TO PROMOTE ARTS AND CULTURE FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE PUBLIC, IN PART BUT NOT EXCLUSIVELY BY:
SUPPORTING YOUNG PERFORMERS;
ORGANISING ART EXHIBITIONS AND CONCERTS FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE PUBLIC TO PROMOTE CHORAL MUSIC, AND;
CREATING OPPORTUNITIES FOR CULTURAL EXCHANGE.

TO PROMOTE SOCIAL INCLUSION FOR THE PUBLIC BENEFIT BY WORKING WITH PEOPLE IN THE LONDON BOROUGH OF NEWHAM AND SURROUNDING AREA WHO ARE SOCIALLY EXCLUDED ON THE GROUNDS OF THEIR ETHNIC ORIGIN (IN PARTICULAR, BUT NOT EXCLUSIVELY, MEMBERS OF SOMALI SPEAKING COMMUNITY) TO RELIEVE THE NEEDS OF SUCH PEOPLE AND ASSIST THEM TO INTEGRATE INTO SOCIETY, IN PARTICULAR BY:
